      "volume3d_dim_body": "A circle fills 78.5% of its square (π⁄4). A sphere fills only 52.4% of its cube (π⁄6). Same shape, same snug fit — but a cube has 8 corners to a square’s 4, and corners are where the round thing isn’t. Keep adding dimensions and the ball all but vanishes: in 10D it catches about 1 dart in 400.",
