      "since_2006_beekeepers_have_reported_lo": "Colony Collapse Disorder (CCD) describes a specific syndrome in which most adult workers disappear while the queen, brood, and food remain. It is not a label for every colony loss. Honey bee health reflects interacting pressures including Varroa and viruses, nutrition and forage, pesticide exposure, weather, queen problems, and management conditions.",
