      "swollen_pink_red_nodules_on_the_roots_": "Swollen pink/red nodules on the roots contain billions of Rhizobium bacteria. These bacteria have an enzyme called nitrogenase that breaks the triple bond of atmospheric N₂ — one of the strongest chemical bonds in nature.",
      "tea_bags": "Tea bags",
      "the_companion_planting_of_corn_beans_a": "The companion planting of corn, beans, and squash — known as milpa in Mesoamerica — is one of humanity's oldest agricultural innovations. Archaeological evidence traces this system to over 7,000 years ago in present-day Mexico. Squash was domesticated ~10,000 years ago, maize ~9,000 years ago from the wild grass teosinte, and common beans ~7,000 years ago.",
      "the_edge_between_two_ecosystems_is_the": "The edge between two ecosystems is the most productive zone.",
      "the_fungus_extends_the_plant_s_root_sy": "The fungus extends the plant's root system by 100-1000×, accessing water and phosphorus the roots can't reach. In return, the plant shares 10-30% of its photosynthesized sugars. Both benefit — neither survives as well alone.",
      "the_golden_ratio_3_parts_brown_carbon_": "The golden ratio: 3 parts Brown (carbon) to 1 part Green (nitrogen). Keep moist like a wrung-out sponge!",
      "the_haudenosaunee_iroquois_confederacy": "The Haudenosaunee (Iroquois Confederacy) call these plants De-oh-há-ko — \"they sustain us.\" The Three Sisters are spiritual beings and precious gifts, central to Haudenosaunee language, ceremony, songs, and cosmology. This is not merely a farming technique — it is a living relationship between people and plants.",
      "the_milpa_system_diffused_northward_ov": "The milpa system diffused northward over millennia, appearing in North America around 1070 CE. By the time European colonizers arrived around 1500, it was a foundational food system across Central and North America.",
