      "the_three_sisters_de_oh_h_ko_meaning_t": "The Three Sisters (De-oh-há-ko, meaning “they sustain us” in Haudenosaunee) is a 7,000-year-old agricultural system originating in Mesoamerica. Indigenous agricultural science developed sophisticated polyculture techniques millennia before modern ecology.",
      "the_three_sisters_go_in_now_after_soil": "The Three Sisters go in NOW after soil reaches 60°F",
