      "annual_62_72k_6g_pipe_qual_is_the_big_": "Annual $62-72K. 6G pipe qual is the big milestone.",
      "annual_70_80k_pension_begins_vesting_a": "Annual ~$70-80K. Pension begins vesting at 5 years employment.",
      "annual_72_82k_approaching_journey_rate": "Annual $72-82K. Approaching journey rate.",
      "annual_75_95k_pension_is_yours_regardl": "Annual $75-95K. Pension is yours regardless of future moves. Healthcare excellent.",
      "annual_90_120k_typical_top_earners_120": "Annual $90-120K typical. Top earners $120-150K with travel work. Defined-benefit pension.",
      "annual_income_60_70k_with_regular_ot_c": "Annual income ~$60-70K with regular OT. Comfortable life in Bath area.",
      "answer_3_quick_questions_we_ll_show_yo": "Answer 3 quick questions. We'll show you the welders whose paths fit your answers best — not the only fits, just the closest matches in this set of 14.",
      "anti_fatigue_mats_on_concrete_floor": "• Anti-fatigue mats on concrete floor.",
      "any_non_porous_material_common_on_stai": "Any non-porous material. Common on stainless steel, aluminum, nickel alloys. Not useful on porous materials (cast iron).",
      "api_1104": "API 1104",
      "application_interview_process_drug_tes": "Application + interview process. Drug test + math test typical.",
      "application_windows_are_tight_usually_": "Application windows are tight (usually 1-2 weeks each year). Selection is competitive (aptitude test + interview). Once in, you cannot easily switch. Travel is common (jobs follow construction). Pay scales formally each year — you know exactly what you'll earn through journey-out. Pension + healthcare are gold-standard. Many of the highest-paid welders in Maine are pipefitters + boilermakers.",
      "apprenticeship": "Apprenticeship",
      "apprenticeship_union_sponsored": "Apprenticeship (union sponsored)",
      "approximately_50_65_pass_on_first_atte": "Approximately 50-65% pass on first attempt. Part C (code book) is typically the hardest — many candidates have never used a code book under time pressure. ~$1,150 fee per exam attempt. AWS-approved prep courses ($500-3000) significantly improve pass rates.",
      "arc_burns_the_retina_in_seconds_galvan": "Arc burns the retina in seconds. Galvanized fumes cause \"zinc fume fever.\" Stainless fumes are a known carcinogen (hexavalent chromium). Hot-work sparks travel 30+ feet and smolder for hours. Every PPE rule below has a body count behind it.",
      "arc_dissociates_water_into_h_o_if_the_": "Arc dissociates water into H₂ + O₂. If the gas pocket gets trapped (hull cavity, pipe), it can detonate. Multiple recorded fatalities. Procedures include venting cavities before lighting up.",
      "arc_efficiency": "Arc Efficiency",
      "arc_flash_bystander_exposure": "Arc Flash / Bystander Exposure",
      "arc_flash_eye_protection_beyond_wear_a": "👁 Arc flash + eye protection — beyond \"wear a hood\"",
